    "explanation": "The age of a contusion can be assessed based on its color\nchanges.\nIts size gradually decreases from the periphery toward the\ncenter. The contusion undergoes a series of color changes\ndue to the disintegration of the red blood corpuscles and the\nliberation of hemoglobin.\nThe color transitions are as follows:\n• Initially, a fully developed contusion appears red or\nsometimes purple\n• By 4 to 5 days, the color transitions to green\n• By 7 to 10 days, it turns yellow and progressively\nfades\n• Typically disappears on 14th or 15th day\nThe total duration for ultimate disappearance of color ranges\nfrom one to four weeks, depending on the severity of the injury\nand individual body constitution.\nThe color changes progress from the periphery inward.",
