    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Stagnant anoxic death, a type of asphyxia death, occurs due\nto failure of circulation. Conditions that may cause stagnant\nanoxic death include:\n• Heart failure\n• Shock\n• Arterial and venous obstruction: incident to embolism,\nvascular spasm, varicose veins, or the use of\ntourniquet\nOther types of asphyxia death are as follows:\n(Choice A) Anemic anoxic death is due to a decreased\ncapacity of the blood to carry oxygen. The decreased capacity\nmay be due to the following:\n• Severe hemorrhage\n• Poisoning, like carbon monoxide\n• Low hemoglobin level in the blood\n(Choice C) Histotoxic anoxic death occurs when there is a\nfailure of the cellular oxidative process. In this type of death,\noxygen is not utilized properly, even if it reaches the tissues.\n(Choice D) Anoxic Death occurs when arterial blood fails to\nachieve normal oxygen saturation. This may result from:\n• Insufficient oxygen in the atmosphere, such as at high\naltitudes.\n• Airway obstruction due to external pressure, as seen\nin traumatic crush asphyxia.\n• Paralysis of the respiratory center, caused by\npoisoning, injury, or anesthesia.\n• Mechanical interference with airflow into or within the\nrespiratory tract (smothering, choking, pneumonia,\nasthma)\n• Blood bypassing the lungs due to congenital\nanomalies, such as a patent foramen ovale.",
