    "id": "medqbank-legal-medicine-0025",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 25,
    "stem": "The following are elements necessary\nto meet the legal definition of informed\nconsent, EXCEPT:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Awareness of possible\nalternative courses of action"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Familiarity with the risks of the\nproposed and alternative\ncourses of action"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Being informed of the chances\nof success or failure of the\nproposed and alternative\ntherapies"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "None of the above"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Satisfaction of the legal definition of \"informed consent\"\nrequires the minimum of five elements of understanding on\nthe part of the patient, namely:\n• Patient must understand the nature of his condition\n• Patient must understand the nature of the proposed\ntreatment or procedure\n• Awareness of possible alternative courses of action\n• Familiarity with the risks of the proposed and\nalternative courses of action\n• Being informed of the chances of success or failure of\nthe proposed and alternative therapies",
