    "explanation": "In mugging, the assailant standing at the back strangles the\nvictim using the forearm applied in front of the neck.\nIn garroting, a ligature, a metal collar, or a bowstring is\napplied around the neck and tightened at the back.\nThrottling is a form of asphyxial death wherein the\nconstricting force applied to the neck is the hand.\nIn burking, the murderer kneels or sits on the victim’s chest,\nand uses his hand to close the mouth and nostrils of the victim.",
