    "correctChoice": null,
    "explanation": "Natural\nThe manner of death refers to the explanation of how the\ncause of death came about. It describes the circumstances\nthat led to the fatal event and may be classified as either\nnatural or violent.\nNatural Death – A death is considered natural when it results\nsolely from disease processes, such as lobar pneumonia,\nruptured tubal pregnancy, cancer, or cerebral hemorrhage due\nto hypertension\nViolent or Unnatural Death – A death is considered violent or\nunnatural when it results from an injury or external force, such\nas gunshot wounds, stab wounds, fractures, or traumatic\nshock.",
