    "id": "medqbank-legal-medicine-0077",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 77,
    "stem": "While working in the emergency room,\nyou discover that Timmy is a victim of\nchild abuse. Under Presidential Decree\nNo. 603, within what time frame are you\nrequired to submit a written report of the\nincident?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "24 hours"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "36 hours"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "48 hours"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "72 hours"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "According to Article 166 of the Child and Youth Welfare Code\n(P.D. 603), all hospitals, clinics, institutions, and private\nphysicians must report in writing any case of child abuse,\nmaltreatment, or labor exploitation within 48 hours of\ndiscovering the case.\nThe report must be submitted to the city or provincial fiscal, the\nLocal Council for the Protection of Children, or the nearest\nDepartment of Social Welfare unit.\nThe receiving agency is then responsible for forwarding the\nreport to the city or provincial fiscal.",
