    "explanation": "Analysis of the blood is the most widely accepted way to\ndetermine the concentration of alcohol in the body.\nThis is a direct method of estimation but the subject may refuse\nblood extraction for such analysis.\nOther possible specimens include:\n• Analysis of the Breath\no Basis of the analysis is that there is a constant\nratio between the concentration of alcohol in\nthe blood stream and in the alveolar air\n• Analysis of the Urine: no widespread use because of\nvariability in the different periods of alcohol intake\n• Analysis of Saliva, Perspiration and Spinal Fluid:\nseldom done.",
