    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Legal medicine, also known as forensic medicine, is the correct answer. It is a branch of medicine that applies scientific knowledge and skills to medicolegal principles. It involves the application of medical expertise in legal contexts, such as in criminal investigations, court proceedings, and the determination of causes of death. Legal medicine plays a crucial role in the interface between medicine and law, assisting in the administration of justice.",
