    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0033",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 33,
    "stem": "Jojo is diagnosed with end-stage cancer and is requesting drugs for his pain. The principle in the management of Jojo's pain is:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Maleficence"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Justice"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Autonomy"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Beneficence"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Beneficence is the principle of acting in the best interest of the patient and promoting their well-being. In Jojo's case, the management of his pain with appropriate drugs aligns with the principle of beneficence, as it aims to alleviate suffering and improve his quality of life during his illness.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Maleficence refers to the principle of doing harm or acting with intent to injure or cause harm to others. In the context of medical ethics, maleficence is considered unethical, as it goes against the principle of beneficence, which emphasizes doing good and promoting the well-being of patients.",
      "B": "Justice in healthcare involves fairness and equity in the distribution of healthcare resources, treatments, and services. It ensures that all individuals have equal access to healthcare without discrimination based on factors such as race, gender, socioeconomic status, or medical condition.",
      "C": "Autonomy refers to the principle of respecting the right of individuals to make their own decisions about their healthcare, based on their values, beliefs, and preferences. In the case of Jojo, respecting his autonomy means honoring his decision to request pain management drugs for his end-stage cancer.",
      "D": "Beneficence is the principle of acting in the best interest of the patient and promoting their well-being. In Jojo's case, the management of his pain with appropriate drugs aligns with the principle of beneficence, as it aims to alleviate suffering and improve his quality of life during his illness."
    },
