    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0055",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 55,
    "stem": "Crime is higher in the following situations, EXCEPT:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Absence of security"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Vulnerable victim"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Presence of guardians"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Motivated offender"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "The presence of guardians, such as law enforcement officers, security personnel, or vigilant community members, acts as a deterrent to criminal behavior. Guardianship can help prevent crime by increasing the perceived risk of detection and apprehension for offenders.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "The absence of security measures, such as surveillance cameras, security guards, or alarm systems, can create opportunities for criminal activities to occur. Criminals may perceive locations with lax security as easy targets, leading to higher crime rates in such situations.",
      "B": "Vulnerable victims, such as individuals who are elderly, disabled, or otherwise unable to defend themselves, may be targeted by offenders due to their perceived inability to resist or report crimes. Crimes against vulnerable victims can include theft, fraud, abuse, and exploitation.",
      "C": "The presence of guardians, such as law enforcement officers, security personnel, or vigilant community members, acts as a deterrent to criminal behavior. Guardianship can help prevent crime by increasing the perceived risk of detection and apprehension for offenders.",
      "D": "A motivated offender refers to an individual who possesses the desire, inclination, and opportunity to commit a crime. Motivated offenders may be driven by various factors, including financial gain, revenge, thrill-seeking behavior, or personal grievances. The presence of motivated offenders contributes to the occurrence of crime, especially in environments where opportunities are available and risks are perceived to be low."
    },
