    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0060",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 60,
    "stem": "The Board of Medical Education has the following functions, EXCEPT:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "To approve hospitals for the training of students"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Prescribe minimum physical facilities and faculty for colleges of medicine"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Prepare the subjects for the physician licensure examination"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Prescribe minimum requirements for admission into medical school"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Typically, the preparation of subjects for physician licensure examinations falls under the jurisdiction of licensing bodies or the Board of Medicine rather than the Board of Medical Education. Licensing bodies develop and administer licensure examinations to assess the competency of medical graduates and ensure that they meet the necessary requirements to practice medicine safely and effectively.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "The Board of Medical Education often plays a role in approving hospitals and other healthcare facilities for the training of medical students. This ensures that students receive appropriate clinical exposure and experience under the supervision of qualified healthcare professionals.",
      "B": "The board is responsible for setting standards regarding the physical infrastructure and faculty qualifications for colleges of medicine. These standards help ensure that medical education institutions provide adequate resources and faculty expertise to support quality medical education and training.",
      "C": "Typically, the preparation of subjects for physician licensure examinations falls under the jurisdiction of licensing bodies or the Board of Medicine rather than the Board of Medical Education. Licensing bodies develop and administer licensure examinations to assess the competency of medical graduates and ensure that they meet the necessary requirements to practice medicine safely and effectively.",
      "D": "The Board of Medical Education may establish minimum requirements for admission into medical schools. These requirements could include academic qualifications, standardized test scores, prerequisite coursework, and other criteria to ensure that prospective medical students possess the necessary knowledge, skills, and aptitude to succeed in medical education and training."
    },
