    "explanation": "Contrary to the provided information, the Medical Act of 1959 does not specify that a candidate for appointment to the Board of Medical Examiners should be the dean of a College of Medicine. Instead, the Act outlines requirements related to citizenship, medical registration, practice experience, moral character, and lack of pecuniary interest in medical schools or institutions.",
