    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0068",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 68,
    "stem": "Juan was apprehended for driving under the influence. At what blood level of alcohol do you expect the driver will have impaired judgment?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "0.08%"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "0.2%"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "0.1%"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "0.06%"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "This is correct. A blood alcohol concentration of 0.1% indicates a high level of intoxication. At this level, individuals typically exhibit impaired judgment, decreased inhibitions, and diminished control. They may also experience difficulty with coordination and reaction time, making driving unsafe.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "A blood alcohol concentration (BAC) of 0.08% is the legal limit for driving in many jurisdictions. At this level, individuals typically experience impaired judgment, decreased inhibitions, and diminished attention and control. It is considered unsafe to operate a motor vehicle with a BAC at or above this level due to the increased risk of accidents.",
      "B": "A blood alcohol concentration of 0.2% represents a significantly high level of intoxication. At this level, individuals may experience severe impairment of judgment, coordination, and motor skills. It is well beyond the legal limit for driving and poses a significant risk to the individual and others on the road.",
      "C": "This is correct. A blood alcohol concentration of 0.1% indicates a high level of intoxication. At this level, individuals typically exhibit impaired judgment, decreased inhibitions, and diminished control. They may also experience difficulty with coordination and reaction time, making driving unsafe.",
      "D": "A blood alcohol concentration of 0.06% represents a moderate level of intoxication. While individuals may experience some effects of alcohol, such as relaxation and decreased inhibitions, judgment impairment may not be as pronounced as at higher BAC levels. However, it is still unsafe to operate a motor vehicle with this level of alcohol in the bloodstream."
    },
