    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0069",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 69,
    "stem": "If the alcohol level of an individual is 0.1%, you can expect:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Uninhibition"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Clumsy movement and fuzzy speech"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Impaired judgment"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Impairment of muscle coordination"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Impaired judgment is a significant effect of alcohol intoxication, particularly at a blood alcohol level of 0.1%. Individuals may have difficulty making rational decisions, assessing risks, and understanding the consequences of their actions. This impairment of judgment can lead to risky behaviors and poor decision-making.\nIn summary, option (c) - Impaired judgment - is the most accurate description of the effects associated with a blood alcohol level of 0.1%. While other effects such as clumsy movement and impairment of muscle coordination may also occur, impaired judgment is a significant concern due to its potential impact on decision-making and behavior.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "At a blood alcohol level of 0.1%, individuals may experience a decrease in inhibitions. They may feel more relaxed and uninhibited in social situations. However, this is not the primary effect associated with a BAC of 0.1%.",
      "B": "Clumsy movement and fuzzy speech are common symptoms of alcohol intoxication, especially at a blood alcohol level of 0.1%. At this level, individuals may exhibit difficulty with coordination, resulting in clumsy movements, and their speech may become slurred or unclear.",
      "C": "Impaired judgment is a significant effect of alcohol intoxication, particularly at a blood alcohol level of 0.1%. Individuals may have difficulty making rational decisions, assessing risks, and understanding the consequences of their actions. This impairment of judgment can lead to risky behaviors and poor decision-making.\nIn summary, option (c) - Impaired judgment - is the most accurate description of the effects associated with a blood alcohol level of 0.1%. While other effects such as clumsy movement and impairment of muscle coordination may also occur, impaired judgment is a significant concern due to its potential impact on decision-making and behavior.",
      "D": "Muscle coordination is often impaired with alcohol consumption, and this impairment becomes more pronounced as the blood alcohol level rises. At a blood alcohol level of 0.1%, individuals may experience noticeable difficulty in coordinating movements, such as walking in a straight line or performing fine motor tasks."
    },
