    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0077",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 77,
    "stem": "Who can NOT be a member of the Board of Medical Education?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Representative, Philippine Medical Association"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Student regent"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Chairman, Board of Medicine"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Secretary of Health"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "A student regent typically represents the interests of students within a university or educational institution. While students may have valuable input regarding medical education, they are not typically appointed as members of the Board of Medical Education, which is primarily composed of medical professionals and representatives from relevant regulatory bodies.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "The Philippine Medical Association (PMA) is a professional organization of physicians in the Philippines. A representative from the PMA can be a member of the Board of Medical Education to provide insights and perspectives from the medical community.",
      "B": "A student regent typically represents the interests of students within a university or educational institution. While students may have valuable input regarding medical education, they are not typically appointed as members of the Board of Medical Education, which is primarily composed of medical professionals and representatives from relevant regulatory bodies.",
      "C": "The Chairman of the Board of Medicine, or any equivalent position, plays a crucial role in overseeing medical licensure examinations and regulatory affairs related to medical practice. The Chairman may also serve as an ex officio member of the Board of Medical Education to ensure coordination and alignment between the two boards.",
      "D": "The Secretary of Health, or any equivalent position, is often involved in healthcare policy-making and regulation at the national level. The Secretary of Health may serve as an ex officio member of the Board of Medical Education to provide governmental oversight and ensure alignment with national healthcare priorities."
    },
