    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0085",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 85,
    "stem": "A deliriant is exemplified by:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Shabu"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Marijuana"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Glue sniffing"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Oxycodone"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Glue sniffing involves the inhalation of volatile solvents found in household products such as glue, paint thinner, and aerosol sprays. These solvents contain chemicals like toluene and xylene, which act as central nervous system depressants. Glue sniffing can lead to a range of effects including euphoria, dizziness, hallucinations, and confusion, which are characteristic of deliriant intoxication.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Shabu, also known as methamphetamine hydrochloride, is a powerful stimulant drug that affects the central nervous system. It belongs to the class of drugs known as amphetamines. Shabu stimulates the release of dopamine and norepinephrine, resulting in increased alertness, energy, and euphoria. It is not typically classified as a deliriant but rather as a stimulant.",
      "B": "Marijuana, also known as cannabis, is a psychoactive drug derived from the Cannabis plant. It contains compounds such as THC (tetrahydrocannabinol) and CBD (cannabidiol) that affect the brain and body. Marijuana is primarily known for its euphoric and relaxing effects. While it can cause alterations in perception and cognition, it is not classified as a deliriant.",
      "C": "Glue sniffing involves the inhalation of volatile solvents found in household products such as glue, paint thinner, and aerosol sprays. These solvents contain chemicals like toluene and xylene, which act as central nervous system depressants. Glue sniffing can lead to a range of effects including euphoria, dizziness, hallucinations, and confusion, which are characteristic of deliriant intoxication.",
      "D": "Oxycodone is a potent opioid medication used for the management of moderate to severe pain. It belongs to the class of drugs known as opioid analgesics. Oxycodone acts on opioid receptors in the brain and spinal cord to relieve pain. While it can cause sedation and cognitive impairment, it is not typically classified as a deliriant."
    },
