    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0088",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 88,
    "stem": "According to RA 9165 or the Comprehensive Dangerous Drug Act, identify the prohibited drug from the following list:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Phenobarbital"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Methaqualone"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Benzedrine"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Lysergic acid diethylamide (LSD)"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "LSD is a hallucinogenic drug known for its powerful psychoactive effects, including alterations in perception, mood, and thought processes. Due to its high potential for abuse and its dangerous effects on mental health, it is listed as a prohibited drug under RA 9165. Its production, distribution, sale, and use are strictly prohibited under Philippine law.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Phenobarbital is a barbiturate medication commonly used to treat seizures, anxiety, and sleep disorders. While it is a controlled substance due to its potential for abuse and dependence, it is not listed as a prohibited drug under RA 9165. However, its use and distribution are regulated under Philippine drug laws.",
      "B": "Methaqualone, also known as Quaalude, is a sedative-hypnotic drug that was previously used for the treatment of insomnia and as a muscle relaxant. However, due to its high potential for abuse and addiction, it is classified as a regulated drug under RA 9165. Its production, distribution, sale, and use are strictly regulated under Philippine law.",
      "C": "Benzedrine, also known as amphetamine, is a stimulant medication used to treat attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) and narcolepsy. While it is a controlled substance and regulated under drug laws, it is not specifically listed as a prohibited drug under RA 9165. However, its use and distribution are subject to regulation and control.",
      "D": "LSD is a hallucinogenic drug known for its powerful psychoactive effects, including alterations in perception, mood, and thought processes. Due to its high potential for abuse and its dangerous effects on mental health, it is listed as a prohibited drug under RA 9165. Its production, distribution, sale, and use are strictly prohibited under Philippine law."
    },
