    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0090",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 90,
    "stem": "Which of the following deviates from the societal rights of the patient expected from the government?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "The right to essential healthcare at an affordable cost."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "The presence of a clinic in the next town."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "The right to a safe and healthy workplace."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "To benefit from the disease prevention program."
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "While having a clinic in the next town may contribute to healthcare accessibility, its absence does not necessarily deviate from societal rights. However, patients should have access to healthcare facilities within reasonable proximity to their residence, as outlined in the right to access to health facilities.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "This aligns with the societal rights of patients as outlined in the Magna Carta of Patient's Rights and Obligations Act of 2017. Patients have the right to access quality healthcare without financial barriers.",
      "B": "While having a clinic in the next town may contribute to healthcare accessibility, its absence does not necessarily deviate from societal rights. However, patients should have access to healthcare facilities within reasonable proximity to their residence, as outlined in the right to access to health facilities.",
      "C": "The Patient as the right to a healthy natural workplace environment with adequate supply of safe and potable water and basic sanitation, industrial hygiene, prevention and reduction of exposure to harmful substances, preventive measures for occupational accidents and diseases, and an environment that discourages abuse of alcohol, tobacco and drug use, and the use of other harmful substances.",
      "D": "This aligns with patient rights as patients have the right to access preventive healthcare services, as outlined in the right to access to quality public healthcare."
    },
