    "id": "notion-legal-medicine-0095",
    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 95,
    "stem": "While playing golf, a thunderstorm with lightning appeared, the players should:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Open an umbrella"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Go near the tree for cover"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Crouch down in the lowest position"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Lie down"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "This is the correct choice. If caught in a thunderstorm with lightning while playing golf, it's important to immediately crouch down in the lowest position possible while minimizing contact with the ground. This position helps reduce the risk of being struck by lightning.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "This is not recommended during a thunderstorm with lightning. Carrying an umbrella can increase the risk of being struck by lightning as it acts as a conductor. Therefore, opening an umbrella during a thunderstorm is unsafe and should be avoided.",
      "B": "Seeking shelter under a tree during a thunderstorm is extremely dangerous. Trees can attract lightning strikes due to their height and conductivity. Being near a tree increases the risk of being struck by lightning and should be avoided at all costs.",
      "C": "This is the correct choice. If caught in a thunderstorm with lightning while playing golf, it's important to immediately crouch down in the lowest position possible while minimizing contact with the ground. This position helps reduce the risk of being struck by lightning.",
      "D": "Lying down flat on the ground during a thunderstorm is not recommended. It increases the surface area in contact with the ground, which can increase the risk of a lightning strike. Additionally, lying down does not provide as much protection as crouching in the lowest position."
    },
